        "body": "### Implement approved Auto and Manual decision governance and internal phases\n\n```yaml\nid: P-09b5b828-dcdc-4d06-bee1-19e1787e34f4\npriority: 128\nstatus: Pending\nparent_pending_ids: []\nprocessing_run_id: null\nroot_task_id: T-657e5621-efb8-4c53-8ab9-bdd2a7e6ec69\nrelated_task_id: T-657e5621-efb8-4c53-8ab9-bdd2a7e6ec69\nrelation: blocker\ndepends_on: []\n```\n\nDescription:\n- Implement owner-approved W1 with explicit research, plan, plan review, implementation, checks, review, finding resolution, fixes and re-review inside existing operations. Auto is the default and uses a separate reasoned resolver, an independent critic for significant decisions and an arbiter for substantive disagreement. Manual presents the same questions and recommendations to the owner in chat.\n\nExpected behavior:\n- Both modes preserve task/run identity and accumulated state across explicit switches and resume. Legitimate delegated Auto answers and final specification acceptance retain real agent provenance and bounded authority; Manual retains actual owner evidence. Existing permissions, required checks and current review remain binding. Out-of-authority requests and repeated no-progress disputes or failures escalate one concrete owner question.\n\nRequest classification:\n- other: The owner approves a new delegated decision capability and internal phases; existing manual-only controller acceptance remains a valid completed baseline.\n\nCurrent context:\n- Required W1 foundation for the frozen interview consumer and shared composition, invocation and review consumers. Task124 remains design-only and W2 remains open. Processing researches decomposition, mode/authority evidence, real-agent qualification and dependency placement after the workflow design gate. Completed contracts and terminal controller128 outcomes remain unchanged.\n\nSource:\n- .skill-tree/history/research/plugin-auto-manual-decision.json; .skill-tree/documents/plugin-workflow-decisions.md; actual ow